<title>CANADA: British Columbia to spend C$1.85 billion on plan.</title>
<headline>British Columbia to spend C$1.85 billion on plan.</headline>
<dateline>PRINCE GEORGE, British Columbia 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Columbia Premier Glen Clark said on Thursday that the government would spend C$370 million a year for the next five years as part of a plan to increase employment in the forestry sector.</p>
<p>Of that total, C$300 million a year would come from the Forest Renewal agency that funds silviculture and other programs.</p>
<p>Clark was announcing details of an accord aimed at increasing direct and indirect employment in the forest industry by 39,800 jobs by 2001.</p>
<p>((Reuters Vancouver Bureau (604) 664-7314))</p>
